# Manual Git Only

The user performs every Git operation manually. Cursor must never run Git commands.

## Forbidden Commands

Do not run any of the following, including as part of suggested terminal workflows:

- `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, `git pull`, `git merge`
- `git checkout`, `git switch`, `git reset`, `git rebase`
- `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, `git stash`
- Any command that creates, deletes, or changes branches
- Any command that modifies Git history or Git configuration

## Required Behavior

- Do not stage, commit, push, merge, or switch branches.
- Do not update `.git/config` or any Git hooks.
- When work is complete, summarize changes and suggest a commit message for the user to apply manually.
- Never claim that changes have been committed or pushed.
